Power manager on tv-emu's virtual machine

The VM has no thermal zone and no CPU frequency scaling, which is what the
Pi's power states act on: without the governor's file the component does not
start, and no power state can be set. Both are files of the virtual device:
/run/tvemu/temperature, in thousandths of a degree, and
/run/tvemu/scaling_governor.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [tv-emu virtual machine]

diff --git a/source/plat-power.c b/source/plat-power.c
index f506bba..f73695b 100644
--- a/source/plat-power.c
+++ b/source/plat-power.c
@@ -69,7 +69,10 @@ schedutil:
     Aims to provide a balance between performance and power saving based on real-time system load.
     Generally considered more efficient and responsive compared to other governors.
 */
-#define CPU_FREQ_SCALING_GOVERNOR_PATH "/sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu0/cpufreq/scaling_governor"
+/* tv-emu: the Pi shows its power state in the CPU's frequency governor. The VM
+   has no CPU frequency scaling; the virtual device has the governor as a file,
+   where the state the middleware has set can be read. */
+#define CPU_FREQ_SCALING_GOVERNOR_PATH "/run/tvemu/scaling_governor"
 
 /**
  * @brief Get the CPU frequency scaling governor.
@@ -422,7 +425,8 @@ pmStatus_t PLAT_API_GetWakeupSrc(PWRMGR_WakeupSrcType_t srcType, bool  *enable)
 
 #define CPU_FREQ_SCALING_CUR_FREQ_PATH  "/sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu0/cpufreq/scaling_cur_freq"
 #define CPU_FREQ_SCALING_SETSPEED_PATH  "/sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu0/cpufreq/scaling_setspeed"
-#define THERMAL_ZONE_TEMPERATURE_PATH   "/sys/class/thermal/thermal_zone0/temp"
+/* tv-emu: the VM has no thermal zone; the virtual device has a file. */
+#define THERMAL_ZONE_TEMPERATURE_PATH   "/run/tvemu/temperature"
 
 /* Warning: not tuned; before enabling; finetune these */
 #define NORMAL_CLOCK_SPEED  1000 // value for normal state
